978): the canonical minimum spanning tree (weight, then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position: SpanningTrees’ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":", by Prim on the dense matrix), a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minimum-weight perfect matching on its odd-degree vertices (MatchingModule’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumWeightMatching"},{"type":"text","text":", Galil’s blossom), an Eulerian circuit of their union by Hierholzer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the first vertex, shortcut to the first visit of each vertex (NetworkX"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"christofides"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ChristofidesThreeHalvesApproxMetricTSP"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ChristofidesTsp"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Each piece is pinned, so the tour is: the matching is on the complete graph of the odd"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order (pairs i < j lexicographic), and the circuit’s multigraph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lists the tree edges by position, then the matched pairs in that order. At most 3\/2 × the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shortest tour when the weights satisfy the triangle inequality (not checked)."}],"title":"christofidesTour(weight:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/christofidesTour(weight:)-6qvc8","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"christofidesTour"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"te